      "Santería's cosmology centers on three tiers of spiritual reality: Olodumare (also Olorun or Olofi), the supreme creator deity who is distant and rarely invoked directly; the orisha, divine intermediaries who govern specific domains of nature and human life; and the ancestors (eggun or muertos), deceased family members and ritual elders who guide and protect the living. This structure mirrors Yoruba theology but with Cuban adaptations. Practitioners understand that Olodumare is too vast and remote for direct human approach, delegating interaction with creation to the orisha, who are more accessible, temperamental, and involved in daily affairs.",
