      "Santería posits a complex relationship between destiny (camino or suerte) and free will. Before birth, each person chooses their destiny in consultation with Olodumare, but upon incarnation, they forget this choice. Life's challenges and opportunities are not random but reflections of pre-birth agreements that can be revealed through divination. However, destiny is not deterministic—humans possess agency to improve or worsen their path through moral conduct (iwa), sacrifice, and alignment with their orisha. This philosophy encourages active ritual engagement rather than fatalism: if divination reveals an obstacle, one performs the prescribed ebo to 'sweeten' (endulzar) the path or 'close' (cerrar) negative influences.",
