      "Santería is decentralized and heterogeneous, lacking the institutional structures (clergy hierarchies, councils, doctrinal statements) that standardize world religions. Authority is personal and lineage-based: each rama traces itself to founding priests (Adeshina, Oba Tero, Ferminita Gómez, Asunción Villalonga, and others) whose initiation protocols and divination interpretations differ subtly. Initiates often identify their rama publicly—'I'm from the rama of Adeshina through my madrina who was godchild of…'—to signal pedigree and authenticate practice. Inter-rama disputes over 'correct' ritual procedure, odu interpretation, or orisha attributes are common, with no mechanism for resolution beyond prestige and consensus.",
